WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.134
Arus can capture media straight from your browser.

2
00:00:03.134 --> 00:00:05.265
In Settings, open the Capture tab.

3
00:00:05.265 --> 00:00:08.336
You'll find three steps to install the extension.

4
00:00:08.336 --> 00:00:11.031
First, open your browser's extensions page.

5
00:00:11.031 --> 00:00:12.472
Turn on Developer mode.

6
00:00:12.472 --> 00:00:14.729
Then load the Arus extension folder.

7
00:00:14.729 --> 00:00:17.612
Once it's installed, play a video on any page.

8
00:00:17.612 --> 00:00:21.059
The Download with Arus button appears above the player.

9
00:00:21.059 --> 00:00:26.324
The extension also detects media automatically, so you don't have to hunt for links.

10
00:00:26.324 --> 00:00:31.087
The extension works on the page you're viewing, without leaving the browser.

11
00:00:31.087 --> 00:00:33.970
Click the button to send the download to Arus.

12
00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:38.357
Want it faster? Press Alt Shift A to grab the media under your cursor.

13
00:00:38.357 --> 00:00:41.554
Every download is still handled by Arus on your PC.

14
00:00:41.554 --> 00:00:46.255
The browser helps find the media, while Arus manages the queue and storage.

15
00:00:46.255 --> 00:00:49.702
Just play the video, then pick the button that appears.

16
00:00:49.702 --> 00:00:53.838
Try it once and see how quickly media lands in your download list.

